%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Serpent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 7
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: Scope
    AbilityDescription: 'Hold the left trigger and a magnified view down your own nose opens in
      a round eyepiece beside the flight view - the ship keeps flying exactly as it did - and the
      right trigger becomes the Sniper Shot. The zoom is the trigger''s own depth: an analog dial
      out to a 12 degree field of view, the same at every level. Charge sets the sniper''s
      RECOVERY: the wait between shots, 12s at rest down to 5.4s at Charge 10.'
    Input: 2
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Hunter's Sight
    UpgradeDescription: 'While the scope is up, every rival in range leaves short-lived
      afterimages - its hull frozen where it stood, every quarter second, for one second. A sniper
      round through an afterimage strips the real pilot as if it had hit them. Read from the
      replicated unlock bit; the afterimages are recorded where the strip is decided.'
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: Seed Wall
    AbilityDescription: 'Stopping (the turret stance) or cloaking leaves a seed prism that pulls
      loose prisms into a self-assembling wall around itself, stealing an
      opponent''s prisms as they land. The pattern is a symmetric herringbone of 2:1 bricks with
      a square hole at every cell, spaced so that once shielded the octahedral bricks point long
      vertex at short vertex with a gap between. Mass sets the SIZE and SPACING of the bricks together (SeedWallActionSO.massSizeMultiplierAtFull,
      x1 at rest to x2 at Mass 10, floored at x0.5), snapshotted when the seed is placed. The
      wall steals from its EDGE: loose prisms within reach of an open site beside a brick are
      pulled in, so it grows toward the mass around it and creeps along trails rather than as a
      circle. Space sets that steal reach (x1 at rest to x2 at Space 10). The stance''s seed is
      shielded and its wall grows only while you stay stopped; fly again and it stands as it
      is. The cloak''s seed is SUPER-SHIELDED and its wall keeps growing until that super-shield
      breaks; kill a seed and its wall stops. Every crystal you collect fires a beam at each of
      your growing walls and ripples a shield through it.'
    Input: 7
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Lockdown
    UpgradeDescription: 'Every square hole in your walls whose four surrounding bricks have
      all closed is sealed with a flat DANGER panel, a thin crack short of the shields around it,
      the moment its fourth brick lands. Crystals still only shield the wall. Read from the
      replicated unlock bit.'
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: Cloak / Sniper Shot
    AbilityDescription: 'The right trigger. Unscoped, it CLOAKS: you leave a super-shielded seed
      that grows a Seed Wall and an illusion of your hull where you were, and fly on unseen. Scoped
      (hold the left trigger), it fires the SNIPER SHOT: one hitscan round, a 1.5 degree cone out
      to 3000 units, that destroys every hostile prism inside it - SUPER-SHIELDED mass included -
      and knocks a petal of every element out of each opposing pilot it crosses. The card shows
      whichever the trigger will do. Space sets how far your Seed Walls reach to steal (x1 at rest
      to x2 at Space 10).'
    Input: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Shield Steal
    UpgradeDescription: 'Your Seed Walls also steal an opponent''s SHIELDED prisms from their edge,
      which they otherwise leave alone.'
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: Solid Fuel Pellets
    AbilityDescription: 'Each press burns one solid fuel pellet - a fixed quarter of the fuel
      tank - and every pellet burns for its own duration. Press again while one is still burning
      and a second lights beside it: the burns overlap and each adds the same increment of speed,
      so four pellets at once is four times the effect of one (3x cruise for one, 9x for four). The
      tank holds exactly four pellets and never refills on its own: a pellet comes back for every
      2 s your Seed Wall spends eating your own trail (fly out at cruise in plane with a wall and
      the trail is pulled into it). A pellet burns 6 s at rest. Time sets how long a pellet BURNS
      (ConsumeBoostActionSO.timeDurationMultiplier, x1 at rest to x1.6 at Time 10, floored at
      x0.25), never how fast.'
    Input: 6
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Fifth Pellet
    UpgradeDescription: 'The tank holds FIVE pellets instead of four: each pellet costs a fifth of
      the tank and still burns and boosts exactly as before, so a full overlap is 11x cruise.'
